.TH BYTEKEYS-GUI 1 "October 2026" "ByteKeys 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bytekeys-gui \- ByteKeys control center for keyboard lighting, fans and performance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bytekeys-gui
[\fB\-\-minimized\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIPAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the ByteKeys control center: live temperatures and fan speeds,
performance modes, firmware fan curves, the battery charge limit, and the
brightness, colors, effects, automations and profiles of the keyboard lighting.
It also adds a tray icon with quick controls. Only one instance runs; starting
it again brings the window to the front, so the laptop's vendor "launch key"
(Armoury Crate, NitroSense, OMEN...) can open it through a desktop shortcut.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the background (used when started at login).
.TP
.BI \-\-page " PAGE"
Open
.BR home ,
.BR lighting ,
.BR performance ,
.BR automation ,
.B profiles
or
.BR settings .
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Add simulated keyboards and fans.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Do not use the bytekeysd service (portable mode).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bytekeys (1),
.BR bytekeysd (8)
